messages:
anya (Docs): Heads-up: product will flip the hosted default to `redwood-1-rlhf` on 2026-04-18. We need a short migration microdoc + update all quickstarts and SDK snippets. Who can own the sweep?
harry (Eng): I can do a repo-wide pass. Searching for `redwood-1`, old streaming patterns like `choices[0]`, and `client.stream()`. Will list occurrences and open a branch.
mika (SDK): Important to call out the v1 -> v2 API changes: `client.generate()` -> `client.responses.create()` and streaming is now an async iterator of event objects (no choices array). I'll prepare a concise compatibility snippet for the docs.
anya (Docs): Keep the migration note tiny: show old call -> new call, a shim, and a troubleshooting bullet for the top two errors support sees. Also mention we'll keep the `redwood-1` alias for 30 days.
jess (Support): Please include a 1-paragraph blurb we can paste into tickets. Customers still paste old quickstarts and hit runtime errors. Also collect any customer-provided snippets to avoid breaking them.
tara (Product): We'll keep alias redirect for 30 days and surface a console banner. Docs should recommend explicit model IDs and include rollback guidance for Dedicated customers who pin models.
mika (SDK): Proposed shim to include in docs and SDK tests: ```js
// short transition shim
function generateShim(opts){
  const model = opts.model || 'redwood-1-rlhf';
  return client.responses.create({ model, input: opts.input || opts.prompt });
}
``` I'll attach tests asserting the shim produces the same response shape for simple prompts.
harry (Eng): Found ~14 matches across /docs, /examples, and /tutorials. I'll push a branch with fixes and include a file list in the PR.
anya (Docs): For the quickstart streaming example, use this exact snippet so it stays consistent: ```ts
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'redwood-1-rlhf', input: 'Hello' });
for await (const ev of stream) {
  if (ev.type === 'response.delta') process.stdout.write(ev.delta);
}
``` Keep it minimal and link to the SDK canonical snippet.
mika (SDK): Will include the snippet verbatim in SDK docs so quickstarts can link to it. Draft PR: #3582.
jess (Support): Draft blurb: "Default hosted model changed to redwood-1-rlhf. redwood-1 alias deprecated for 30 days. Update SDK usage to client.responses.create and client.responses.stream. If you need a Dedicated rollback, contact support." I'll post to #support-ready once edited.
anya (Docs): Timeline: open docs PR by 2026-04-13, merge by 2026-04-16 so preview builds are available (deploy window is 2026-04-17). Tag me for final review.
preview-bot: Reminder: request docs preview builds at least 45m before the deploy window. Builds take ~20m.
harry (Eng): Aiming to list all files in the PR description and add changelog line.
mika (SDK): Also adding a small mapping table for old params -> new location (e.g., temperature: old params.temperature -> now top-level temperature). That should reduce support noise.
anya (Docs): Good. I'll add a tiny troubleshooting section: 1) "Missing choices" errors -> point to streaming change; 2) param location errors -> show mapping. That should cut the tickets.
mika (SDK): I'll keep the shim and alias handling active for 30 days in the SDK so rollouts are smoother.
anya (Docs): Perfect. Once PRs are green I'll open the meta PR to add a redirect rule and the changelog entry. Ping here when ready. :rocket:
